---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { breadcrumbs } from '../lib';
import { CHECKED } from '../data/apps';
---
<Base title="About and affiliate disclosure" description="Who runs AppsForBudgeting, how app information is checked, and our affiliate disclosure." jsonLd={[breadcrumbs([{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'About', path: '/about' }])]}>
  <h1>About AppsForBudgeting</h1>
  <p>AppsForBudgeting is a small, independent directory of budgeting apps. We focus on what households with young kids care about: sharing a budget with a partner, keeping costs low, and planning for irregular expenses like childcare.</p>
  <h2>How we check app information</h2>
  <p>Prices and features come from each app’s official website or help center. The current listings were checked in {CHECKED}, and each app page links to the page we used. Apps change their prices often, so always confirm on the official site before you subscribe.</p>
  <p>We don’t publish star ratings or scores yet, because we haven’t finished hands-on testing. We don’t use made-up user counts or testimonials.</p>
  <h2 id="disclosure">Affiliate disclosure</h2>
  <p>Today, AppsForBudgeting has no affiliate relationships and earns nothing when you click a link. If that changes, we’ll say so on this page and next to every affiliate link, and an affiliate relationship won’t change which apps we list or what we say about them.</p>
  <h2>Not financial advice</h2>
  <p>This site gives general information about software. It isn’t financial, legal or tax advice.</p>
</Base>
